## Leaner rule set and safer rules :broom:

This release **removes ~100 rules deprecated in past releases**. They already threw on use, were part of no set and were rarely used. If your `rector.php` still registers one of them, remove it from the config. The goal stays the same: a smaller set of valuable, reliable rules for everyday upgrades.

The rest of the release is about **safer changes** - more than 30 rules now skip or keep code where the change could alter behavior: side effects, evaluation order, loose comparisons, fall-through cases, nullable types and more.

<br>

## New Features :partying_face:

- [CodeQuality] Add `NarrowPreviousExceptionCodeArgRector`, part of code-quality and named-args sets ([#9052](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/9052))

```diff
 try {
     $someCode = 1;
 } catch (Throwable $throwable) {
-    throw new \RuntimeException('ups', $throwable->getCode(), $throwable);
+    throw new \RuntimeException('ups', previous: $throwable);
 }
```

- [Php84] Handle property fetch, static access, array access and invocation on `NewMethodCallWithoutParenthesesRector` ([#9009](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/9009), [#9010](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/9010)) Thanks @alexndlm

```diff
-$message = (new Regex('some-pattern'))->message;
-$constant = (new Request())::METHOD_GET;
-$value = (new ArrayObject($items))['key'];
-$result = (new Invokable())();
+$message = new Regex('some-pattern')->message;
+$constant = new Request()::METHOD_GET;
+$value = new ArrayObject($items)['key'];
+$result = new Invokable()();
```

- [Php71] Convert partial `list()` destruct in `ListToArrayDestructRector` ([#9028](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/9028))

```diff
-list(, $instanceId) = explode(':', $rate->id);
+[, $instanceId] = explode(':', $rate->id);
```

- [TypeDeclaration] Allow `void` on final methods of non-final classes in `AddVoidReturnTypeWhereNoReturnRector` ([#9051](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/9051))

```diff
 abstract class SomeClass
 {
-    final protected function run()
+    final protected function run(): void
     {
         echo 1;
     }
 }
```

- [TypeDeclaration] Use `object` return type for `(object)` cast in `ReturnTypeFromReturnCastRector` ([#9021](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/9021))

```diff
-public function run($data): \stdClass
+public function run($data): object
 {
     return (object) $data;
 }
```

- [CodeQuality] Drop redundant bool cast under negation in `UnnecessaryTernaryExpressionRector` ([#9024](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/9024))

```diff
-return $order ? false : true;
+return !$order;
```

- [dx] Report unnecessary skips in parallel runs too - `->reportUnusedSkips()` now works with the default parallel run, not only with `--debug` or `withoutParallel()` ([#8957](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8957))

<br>

## Bugfixes :bug:

### Core

- Keep the narrowed scope of a ternary branch when a changed node is refreshed ([#9007](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/9007)) Thanks @SanderMuller
- Fix class scope refresh skipping class attributes when class node is already in class ([#9004](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/9004)) Thanks @APX403
- [Core] Skip classes unknown to reflection instead of crashing in `fetchClassLikeReflection()` ([#8965](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8965)) Thanks @hmennen90
- [Caching] Fix removed skip not invalidating cache after `--clear-cache` run ([#8934](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8934))
- [Printer] Wrap compound assign on the left of `instanceof` and binary ops ([#9005](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/9005)) Thanks @odolbeau
- [Php86] Handle crash on partial function application on PHP 8.6 scope set attribute ([#9013](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/9013))

